# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Pages INHERITS the headers of every matching rule and JOINS duplicate
# header names with a comma, so a Cache-Control set under /* is never
# overridden by /assets/* - it is appended to it. A rule for /assets/*
# that only *adds* Cache-Control therefore produces the broken value
# "no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
# (no-store wins, nothing is cached). Prefix the name with "! " to detach
# the inherited value first, then set the one we want.

# HTML is the only thing that must never go stale after a deployment, so the
# no-store policy stays on the catch-all and is detached for long-lived assets.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# Images/graphics are safe to cache for a year. The detached Cache-Control
# below replaces the inherited no-store policy instead of colliding with it.
# `immutable` is deliberately omitted: /assets/profile.jpeg is referenced
# without a ?v= string, so a stale copy would be pinned for a full year after
# any swap. Re-add `immutable` if assets ever get content-hashed filenames.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000
